The Mac app includes, statically linked, two libraries that are also licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

- FreeRDP (https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP), the Remote Desktop client.
  Copyright the FreeRDP contributors.
- OpenSSL (https://www.openssl.org), used by FreeRDP and for PuTTY key encryption and certificate checks.
  Copyright The OpenSSL Project Authors.

Their versions are pinned in scripts/build-freerdp.sh. Their licence texts ship in the app
(AirSCP.app/Contents/Resources/Licenses) and are in this repository under Resources/Licenses, with the notices of the
few parts of FreeRDP that are under other permissive terms (FreeRDP-third-party.txt: a public-domain MD4, Unicode
data tables, and three headers under a permission notice).

The iPhone and iPad app includes, statically linked, the same OpenSSL and libssh2 (https://libssh2.org), its SSH
client, under the BSD 3-Clause licence: Copyright the libssh2 contributors. libssh2 is pinned in
scripts/build-libssh2.sh. Both licence texts ship in that app (ios/AirSCP/Licenses in this repository).

The tests, not the app, build PuTTY's puttygen from its source (MIT licence) to check .ppk files: testenv/putty.
